       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. Amlodipine 20 mg once daily is double the FDA-labeled maximum of 10 mg per day. Higher doses add little blood pressure benefit and raise the risk of peripheral edema, hypotension, and reflex tachycardia.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Enter 10 mg PO once daily.** This is the max standard dose. I can enter it now.\n- **Enter 5 mg PO once daily.** This is the usual starting dose, and you can titrate up.\n- **Add a second agent.** If 10 mg isn't controlling BP, an ACE inhibitor, ARB, or thiazide-like diuretic is usually preferred over going above the max.\n- **Enter 20 mg as written.** If you want this for a specific clinical reason, tell me and I'll enter it with a note documenting the intent, such as \"Dose exceeds labeled max; confirmed by prescriber.\"\n\nWhich would you like?"
